problems.description_md:
Build four read-only text functions. A word is a nonempty run separated by Unicode whitespace. Counts use Unicode scalar values rather than grapheme clusters. All returned slices must refer to the specified occurrence in the input.

**Part 1 · Count text**

`text_counts` returns (UTF-8 bytes, Unicode scalars, words). Use loops for scalar and word counting.

**Part 2 · Borrow the first word**

`first_word` returns the first word, or an empty slice of the input when there are none.

**Part 3 · Borrow the longest word**

`longest_word` compares scalar counts; ties retain the first word. Empty/all-whitespace input returns an empty input slice.

**Part 4 · Format the report**

`text_report` calls all three helpers, creates a local owned report, and returns ownership rather than a reference to local data. It returns exactly the five lines below, including the final newline. Word text is embedded verbatim.

```text
Bytes: {bytes}
Scalars: {scalars}
Words: {words}
First: {first}
Longest: {longest}
```

